.TH DQL-VERSION 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-version \- print build identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql version
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the binary's build identity: version, burned identity (or
.B dev
for local builds), profile, and os/arch, then the SHA-256 of the
running binary on its own line.
.PP
.EX
$ dql version
0.1.0 (dev, debug, linux/aarch64)
binary sha256: 953b7b75c7e9eb7bc1e13f7d690d43824c733f86958ea3a5d77a9971faf5966c
.EE
.PP
With
.B \-\-json
a single-line JSON object is emitted \(em the supply-contract interface
(TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md \(sc11): supplied/CI mode must refuse binaries
whose identity is
.BR dev .
.PP
.EX
$ dql version --json
{"version":"0.1.0","identity":"dev","profile":"debug",
 "os":"linux","arch":"aarch64","fatboy_digests":null,
 "binary_sha256":"953b7b75c7e9eb7..."}
.EE
.PP
.I fatboy_digests
is null on dev builds; release builds carry the adapter digests that
.B dql target verify
checks against.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-target (1)
